lines+=['','![Conditional scales and systematic response versus recorded time](figures/response-versus-time.png)','', '![Source structure and shoulder distortion](figures/source-structure.png)','', 'Warm T10 response-equivalent uncertainties are essentially unchanged: plus peak−0.04%,template+0.28%,aperture+0.71% against current rank10. Its T10 peak/template/aperture change by+0.183/+0.362/+90.1, below0.05 matching control σ, but it is not bitwise the same optimizer solution. Covariance gives plus peak uncertainty+4.08% (worse),template−4.63%,aperture−9.21%; it also changes unperturbed T10 template by−1.21% and aperture by−4.06%, and narrows the major FWHM10.1376→9.9991arcsec. Its shoulder recovery is84.56% versus84.28%. These mixed changes do not establish a universally better astronomical result. Current rank15 offers lower compact scales but worse shoulder recovery81.62%, as in the prior rank record.','', 'At equalN, neither candidate has a measured raw-to-result speed advantage. At comparable achieved compact/broad checkpoint quality, warm N5 closely matches current N5 but recorded prefix readiness is92.84 versus77.83s; its plateau is no earlier. Covariance is not equivalent to the control’s source shape/extended measurement and has the N7 shape excursion. We do not convert faster kernel time into an unmeasured adjusted wall time or invent a numerical operational POINT deadline. No such deadline was supplied.','', '## Numerical and support evidence','', 'All1,320 saved native segment records converge, preserve original eligibility and retain every admitted entry, with zero application failed times. Each trajectory uses six original segments per network; admitted detector populations are417(network11) and411(network12), with594 or610 scheduled rows per segment. Exact detector lists, original slot intervals, eligibility hashes, realized ranks and complete support-audit planes are in native-methods.json and SUPPORT records. Candidate map HITS,NORMALIZATION,SCI_SUPPORT,NORM_SUPPORT and WCS agree on the full grids, before common-domain response diagnostics. No lost coverage is hidden by a smaller comparison denominator.','', 'Warm state is branch/run/network/segment/rank/scope-bound, immediately previous and converged; current means,coefficients,objective and full stopping criterion are recomputed. No cold rescue. Its REF projector differences from current REF span0.00190–0.43973 in Frobenius norm. Covariance differences span0.00539–1.98738; later maps have different residual operands, so these are method-state differences, not fixed-input equivalence tests. Signed full eigenspectra, pair-count distributions, objectives and native timings are retained.','', 'At T10, summed observed-entry residual objectives are1.321089e11(current10),1.320973e11(warm10),1.336068e11(covariance10), and1.113727e11(current15), each over2,870,933 eligible entries. Corresponding detector-time residual RMS values are214.513,214.504,215.726 and196.960mJy/nominal beam. Full objective histories are retained per network/segment/cycle. Later residual operands differ, so lower objective is not a paired fixed-input or map-quality proof; covariance is not optimizing the same low-rank SSE.','', 'Covariance pair overlaps span213–610 samples, above the rank10 minimum11. REF eigen residuals are at most4.38e−15, below the declared100ε×detector-count tolerance. Negative eigenvalue mass reaches0.404% of positive power; it is retained, not clipped. Selected modes are largest positive algebraic eigenvalues, with current validity-aware coefficients. J=0 does not claim an observed-entry SSE minimizer. Complete-data PCA equivalence, masked NaN handling, indefinite covariance, unavailable overlap/rank, warm scope/mask/tolerance and dependency failures have focused synthetic tests.','', 'No unexpected native error-level log lines were found. Existing NumPy matmul runtime warnings are retained in the logs and census; all saved accepted measurement vectors and supported conditional endpoint scales were checked finite. This check does not erase the warning or constitute platform-wide numerical qualification.','', 'The peak recorded storage snapshot was17.51GB against a93.44GB allocation ceiling. Snapshots plus explicit reservations are not a continuous filesystem high-water measurement. Compact preservation removes only exact enumerated inactive detector-time scratch after verified durable commit and review.','', '## Disposition, provenance and reproduction','', 'Phase C: **deliberately unselected**. One next bounded action: remove campaign-size dependence from storage accounting and measure the large adapter/provenance costs while preserving exact scientific results; then design fresh matched timing evidence before independent-observation qualification. No RTC change, further FRUIT-method work, automatic stopping, new observations/arrays, integration, push or production activation occurred.','', 'Phase A science: e28f6630fffaba77f78fc2c2cb883c7345ad92f4, exact independent preflight pass. Its timing report was committed at b7746e3ca6f1615039a2b9d4a3aabe2df62a2a7f before candidate implementation. Phase B science:08f81382d96afb0aad6bc1ed40543322887729b9, tree09005e5f5d36be6ae00267e3341adab9ee080ac6, independent preflight pass. Both executables matched their clean source revisions. Original frozen tag/profile remain unchanged.','', 'The small comparison records, maps, all-cycle measurements, native diagnostics, timing/configuration hashes, figures and manifests are preserved locally. Redundant repeat arrays are unnecessary for reporting. Reporting scripts read saved maps/measurements; no original-input processing, new endpoint ensemble or native solver is run. Extraction of basis diagnostics happened before native cleanup, and its machine-readable result is retained. See ../../REPRODUCTION.md for exact saved-only commands, tests, cleanup and review boundaries.']
